# Attachment upload = encrypt.lu single Blob + relay

Do **not** reintroduce HTTP chunking for new uploads.

## What encrypt.lu does (verified from their bundle + relay)

1. `POST /api/init-upload` → `{ transferId, uploadToken }`
2. One ciphertext Blob
3. Safari: XHR `PUT /api/upload/:id` + Bearer, then PUT + `?uploadToken=` (no POST)
4. Chrome: fetch PUT + Bearer, then PUT/POST + query token
5. Blob without `Content-Type`; warm-up GET to the relay
6. Page: **no COEP/COOP**
7. Relay CORS: `Allow-Origin` + `Allow-Headers: authorization` + methods — **no** `Allow-Credentials`

## PrivateNote mapping

| encrypt.lu | PrivateNote |
|---|---|
| `relay.encrypt.lu` | `upload.privatenote.ai` / `upload-staging.privatenote.ai` |
| `POST /api/init-upload` | `POST /api/notes/reserve` |
| `PUT /api/upload/:id` | `PUT /api/notes/:id/file` |

SPA upload surface must not send `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` (keep COEP only on `/llm-ui` + `/test-llm`).
